> **SELF-EXCLUSION.** Grok 5 is **not publicly released** and publishes **zero verified benchmark numbers**, so no 1–100 scores are filed here — placeholder scores would drag the mean for every reader. The notes below record what is verifiable and what is still unconfirmed; nothing in this file is scored.

## Model card (verified facts only)

- **Name:** Grok 5
- **Short description:** xAI's still-unreleased next flagship — reportedly training in two MoE variants (6T and 10T parameters) on the Colossus 2 gigawatt supercluster and positioned as the successor to the Grok 4.x line. No public weights, API ID, price or evaluation exists.
- **Provider / access:** Not released. No public API, no OpenCode Zen ID, no weights. Prior Q1-2026 and Q2-2026 launch windows both closed without a launch; third-party trackers point to Q3 2026 or later.
- **Release / knowledge:** Unreleased (as of 2026-10-01). xAI publicly confirmed the training run on 2026-01-06 alongside its Series E raise; no official release date has ever been announced. Knowledge cutoff not applicable.
- **IDs:** None verified. Community usage of `grok-5` is speculative.
- **Context window:** Not confirmed. Community expectation is only that it "exceeds Grok 4's 2M tokens" — unverified.
- **Modalities:** Not confirmed (expected text; broader multimodality unconfirmed).
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-01):** Not announced. Only consumer-subscription speculation (SuperGrok $30/mo, SuperGrok Heavy $300/mo) exists — not a token price.
- **Architecture:** Reportedly Mixture-of-Experts, training in ~6T and ~10T parameter variants on Colossus 2 (gigawatt-scale, Memphis). All figures are vendor-adjacent reporting, not a published spec sheet.

